  not-modeled.silver-ammine-ligand-inventory  (kerotakis-phreeqc/aqueous.rs)  = "Silver-ammonia equilibrium complexes and free ligand are represented in the solution speciation. The canonical NH3/NH4 portions remain analytical total-nitrogen carriers, including complex-bound ammonia; they are not measured free NH3 amounts. Their use for downstream ammonia volatilisation or curated reaction availability is not yet reconciled with bound ligand. This limitation does not withdraw the reported equilibrium complex distribution"
  not-modeled.analytical-component-charge  (kerotakis-phreeqc/aqueous.rs)  = "the supplied inventory has uncompensated ionic charge. This adapter interprets non-H/O element totals as an analytical component problem and adjusts pH to impose electroneutrality; H/O basis entries are conservation coordinates, not prescribed free-ion concentrations. A reported pH or speciation therefore describes that proton-compensated analytical problem, not a prediction for a complete physical mixture of these ions. Supply the actual counterions or use complete acid, base or salt reagents; no sodium, chloride or other counterion is inferred"
  not-modeled.bare-acid-base-basis  (kerotakis-phreeqc/aqueous.rs)  = "this solvent-only inventory contains explicit acid/base equivalents. Their neutralisation, water balance and reaction heat are not implemented by the solvent autoionisation path. The inventory is retained and no solution reading is assigned; use complete acid/base reagents for a supported neutralisation experiment"
  routing.silver-ammine  (kerotakis-phreeqc/aqueous.rs)  = "chosen because silver and reduced nitrogen require the silver-ammonia complexes present in minteq.v4.dat (NIST46.4 entries 204901 and 204902); elemental coverage in the default dataset does not include these ligand species"
